{"item_id":"E-RES-626","ledger":[{"claim_id":"Q01","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"Turn the abstract topic into a bounded Bareni workflow decision. Explain one practical next step."},{"source_id":"C01","quote":"The representative pains are 8–10 hours a week of repeated customer questions, neglected sales leads,
  and manual invoice/data work."}],"rationale":"This is a drafting instruction to open with an illustrative scenario, not an assertion that such a case was observed at a customer. The named examples (support categorization, invoice approval, lead scoring) align with the persona pains and Bareni's workflow scope.","use_guidance":"Keep explicitly proposed and clearly hypothetical: label the scenario as an example or persona situation, never as an observed customer case, deployment, or result. Do not attach numbers such as 8–10 hours as a market statistic or measured outcome."},{"claim_id":"Q02","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"Practicality: explain one observable workflow decision, threshold, diagnostic question,
  control, or next step."},{"source_id":"C05","quote":"Prefer concrete mechanisms and measured outcomes."}],"rationale":"An instruction about how to frame the explanation for the owner reader, not a factual claim about Bareni capabilities or customer experience.","use_guidance":"Keep as a proposed explanatory frame. Present causes (workflow change, tool change, shifted behaviour) as generic possibilities, not as diagnosed events at any real business, and avoid invented failure statistics."},{"claim_id":"Q03","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"Decision context: the owner compares a bounded automation investment with continuing
  manual work or hiring; final approval and business authority remain human."},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"The diagnostic identifies the one recurring workflow, says honestly whether AI
  fits, and—if it does—defines pilot scope, fixed price, and measures."}],"rationale":"A planned content element presenting decision options to the reader; it asserts no current implementation or observed benefit. Manual override and honest fit assessment sit within approved positioning.","use_guidance":"Keep proposed. Describe option costs qualitatively; do not quote prices, timings as guarantees, or effort figures that are not in the evidence, and keep human decision authority with the owner."},{"claim_id":"Q04","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"Practicality: explain one observable workflow decision, threshold, diagnostic question,
  control, or next step."}],"rationale":"An explicit diagnostic question for the reader, which the persona focus permits; illustrative percentages are framed as question wording rather than measured facts.","use_guidance":"Keep proposed and use only one such question. Present the 5%/30% figures as an illustrative threshold the owner would estimate himself, not as a Bareni benchmark or observed frequency."},{"claim_id":"Q05","category":"QUALIFICATIONS","evidence":[{"source_id":"C02","quote":"Normal sequence: free 30-minute diagnostic; free one-page pilot proposal;
  paid working MVP in days; fixed-price pilot in weeks"},{"source_id":"C04","quote":"Bareni currently declines high-sensitivity medical, legal, and financial work;
  bulk cold-email automation; scan-heavy OCR-dependent workflows"},{"source_id":"C01","quote":"Especially suitable businesses already work in English, use digital
  documents and SaaS tools, and have a frequent, repeatable workflow with a
  measurable outcome."}],"rationale":"The proposed next step (document the real rule and failing cases) is permissible, but the claim also asserts as fact that this documentation feeds a pilot proposal, which is only true within the approved sequence and scope limits. The conditions stated in the claim omit the scan-heavy/OCR exclusion and the digital-document fit condition.","use_guidance":"Add the missing conditions before use: state that the pilot proposal follows the free diagnostic and free one-page proposal step, that scan-heavy or OCR-dependent and high-sensitivity workflows are currently out of scope, and that timings are intended scopes rather than guarantees. Keep the explicit statement that this is not proof of automation fit."},{"claim_id":"Q06","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"**CTA rule:** None."},{"source_id":"C05","quote":"Informational posts use no CTA or one soft closing sentence."}],"rationale":"An instruction for a neutral closing line with an explicit prohibition on any CTA; it makes no factual capability claim.","use_guidance":"Keep proposed and enforce the no-CTA rule: no booking prompt, meeting invitation, offer to discuss, or capacity/scarcity line. End with the neutral practical observation only."}]}

